<p>I actually feel like the Foundation wouldn't do this, since it'd breed distrust and resentment. Establishing a good rapport with the anomalous entity so that cooperation and trust is achieved is a good thing.</p>
<p>I mean, if you had containment as consisting of three trained female personnel effectively assigned to be roommates with Elena in some nice little isolated cottage somewhere, I would be okay with that. The containment procedures make a lot more sense since they keep the anomaly's interference with Foundation activity to a minimum, and also makes her less likely to just want to up and break out.</p>
